TrueVision3D - the Layer flyout and reference layers
  PASS  a layer from before reference layers comes out of the normaliser byte-identical
  PASS  a reference layer keeps Layer__Selectable false
  PASS  true, or anything else, is not stored: selectable is every layer's default
  PASS  IsLayerSelectable: a layer with no key, and a layer the sheet does not have, are both selectable
  PASS  Ref on: the record stores false, it reads unselectable, and it is announced once as layers
  PASS  Ref off: the key comes off the record again
  PASS  Ref on takes its items out of the selection: the line on it, and the group all of whose members are on it; the rest stay
  PASS  only the sheet being worked on is trimmed: an id on another sheet names another record
  PASS  hiding a layer trims the selection too, as Blender deselects what it hides; a group with a member still shown stays
  PASS  ItemLayerId reads every layered kind, and null for a group or an item that is gone
  PASS  every kind moves at once - a viewport under its own lock too, as that lock holds its framing, not its layer - and a group record is passed over
  PASS  one announcement for the lot, as layers: one undo step, and the whole sheet restacks
  PASS  moved onto a layer that is shown and selectable, the selection stays as it was
  PASS  nothing to move - everything already there - announces nothing
  PASS  an item on a locked layer stays where it is
  PASS  and a locked layer takes nothing
  PASS  a layer that does not exist takes nothing either
  PASS  a line put away on a HIDDEN layer leaves the selection - no Delete can reach what cannot be seen
  PASS  and one put on a REFERENCE layer leaves it too - it can no longer be picked
  PASS  IsItemPickable: a line on a reference layer no, the drawing's line yes, a group while any member can be picked, an item that is gone yes
  PASS  and a line on a hidden layer no
